#
# A domain object: a thing the code reasons about, detached from the database. A value
# without identity — a money, a date range — is one of these too, and lives in the same
# tree.
#
# **It holds a shape and validates that shape. It computes nothing.** Deriving a value is
# an operation's job, and a shape is not an operation.
#
# **It holds other shapes; it never copies their fields.** `Booking` carrying
# `supplier_name` and `supplier_email` has taken two of `Supplier`'s columns and made them
# its own, and a flattened field is the first column of the next god object.
class Shape
  include TypedArguments

  # **A shape never holds a record.** Stated once, in `HoldsNoRecords`, because a view
  # component is held to the same rule and two copies of one rule is how they diverge.
  extend HoldsNoRecords

  # Value semantics, without a macro. Two shapes of the same class holding the same
  # values are the same shape — which is what lets one be compared, deduplicated and
  # asserted on in a test without anybody writing `==` per class.
  def ==(other)
